{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>ואף גם זאת.</b> An expression of rhetorical force, and one would suffice. So too all of Scripture [uses such doubling]. Likewise הרק אך — but in Moses [there is] no digging of graves." "<b>לא מאסתים לכלותם.</b> But to chastise them until their heart is humbled." "<b>געלתים.</b> I withdrew from them, or my soul loathed them." "<b>להפר בריתי.</b> That I swore to them. And even if they violated my covenant — for so it is written: I will not violate my covenant with them, for I am Elohim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The final phrase וכן הרק אך במשה המבלי אין קברים is textually obscure; read hyper-literally. Possibly corrupt. The reference and syntax are uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:54.864088420Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}